\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every nonnegative initial density on $T^3×R^3$ with compact velocity support and finite mass, kinetic energy and absolute entropy, must the periodic hard-sphere Boltzmann equation have at most one global admissible renormalized solution satisfying the source mass, momentum, energy and entropy conditions, strong L1 continuity and integrable gain and loss on a common initial interval?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every nonnegative initial density on $T^3×R^3$ with compact velocity support and finite mass, kinetic energy and absolute entropy, must the periodic hard-sphere Boltzmann equation have at most one global admissible renormalized solution satisfying the source mass, momentum, energy and entropy conditions, strong L1 continuity and integrable gain and loss on a common initial interval?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
